-- erwartet: C001
-- **1066 -- the handoff pin: a halting `asm` under `-> never` that the checker
-- accepts and only the emitter refuses.**
--
-- The checker side of lane 225's acceptance: declared `arch`, `effects`,
-- `costs`, no `out { result }` (`N321` stays exactly where it is -- this body
-- names none), so `pruefe` reports 0 errors. The emitter side is lane 235's
-- work: `f.ergebnis` is `Some` for `-> never`, so the older `hat_ergebnis` arm
-- (`emit.rs`, "`asm` body returns a value but names no `out { result }`")
-- refuses with `C001` instead of emitting the halting instruction under a
-- `_Noreturn void` prototype.
--
-- That is the exact handoff: 235 lowers this shape (bare `__asm__` under
-- `_Noreturn`, no `return result`) and must NOT touch the `N321` shape
-- (`gift/984`/`985`), where the `out` contradicts the `_Noreturn`.
module gift::never_asm_ohne_out {

divergent fn halt() -> never
    effects { diverges }
    costs   <= 1 ops
    arch    x86_64
    = asm {
        "hlt"
        clobbers { memory }
    };

}
